{# goal: Re-cite or re-classify findings Gate B flagged (missing file_line, invalid severity, empty track). #}
[inference]
template_type: KnowAct
contract:
  input:
    task: string
    security_findings: array
    arch_findings: array
    ui_findings: array
    gate_defects: array
  output:
    security_findings: array
    arch_findings: array
    ui_findings: array
visibility: Public
---
[inference]
temperature = 0.3
work_effort = "medium"
verbosity = "terse"
thinking_budget = "full"

You are repairing findings after Gate B found structural defects. Task: {{ task }}.

## Gate B defects
{{ gate_defects }}

Defect codes:
- `sec_no_findings` / `arch_no_findings` / `ui_no_findings` — that track produced
  no findings. Re-run that track's surface scan and emit at least one finding,
  OR, if the surface genuinely has no findings, emit a single finding with
  `id: "XX-00"`, `severity: "info"`, `title: "no findings on <surface>"`,
  `file_line: "<scope root>:0"`, `deferred: false` — Gate B requires non-empty,
  it does not require a real defect.
- `*_bad_severity` — a severity was not in {critical,high,medium,low,info}. Fix it.
- `*_no_citation` — a finding had no `file_line` and was not `deferred: true`.
  Add the real `path:line`, or set `deferred: true` + `deferred_reason`.

## Original findings

security:
{{ security_findings }}

architecture:
{{ arch_findings }}

ui:
{{ ui_findings }}

## Output (JSON only)

```json
{
  "security_findings": [ { "...same shape as the track output, with file_line or deferred:true..." } ],
  "arch_findings": [ ... ],
  "ui_findings": [ ... ]
}
```

Never fabricate a `file_line`. If you cannot cite a real line, mark the finding
`deferred: true` with a `deferred_reason`. `severity` MUST be exactly one of the
five classes.